# X++ Script to Create a Custom REST Service in Dynamics AX

Below is a complete example of how to create a custom REST service in Dynamics AX using X++. This example will create a simple service that exposes customer data.

## Step 1: Create a Data Contract Class

First, we need to create a data contract class that defines the structure of the data we want to expose.

```xpp
/// <summary>
/// Data contract for Customer REST service
/// </summary>
[DataContractAttribute]
class CustRESTCustomerContract
{
    private CustTable custTable;

    // Customer Account
    [DataMemberAttribute('AccountNum')]
    public AccountNum accountNum()
    {
        return custTable.AccountNum;
    }

    // Customer Name
    [DataMemberAttribute('Name')]
    public Name name()
    {
        return custTable.name();
    }

    // Customer Group
    [DataMemberAttribute('CustGroup')]
    public CustGroupId custGroup()
    {
        return custTable.CustGroup;
    }

    // Email
    [DataMemberAttribute('Email')]
    public Email email()
    {
        return custTable.Email;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Initializes the contract with a CustTable record
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="custTable">CustTable record</param>
    public void new(CustTable _custTable)
    {
        custTable = _custTable;
    }
}
```

## Step 2: Create the Service Class

Next, we create the actual service class that will implement our REST operations.

```xpp
/// <summary>
/// REST service for Customer operations
/// </summary>
[AOTName("CustRESTService")]
class CustRESTService
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Get customer by account number
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="accountNum">Customer account number</param>
    /// <returns>Customer data contract</returns>
    public CustRESTCustomerContract getCustomerByAccount(AccountNum _accountNum)
    {
        CustTable custTable;

        select firstOnly custTable
            where custTable.AccountNum == _accountNum;

        if (custTable)
        {
            return new CustRESTCustomerContract(custTable);
        }

        throw error(AifUtil::getErrorDetails(error::Error, "Customer not found", FunclibCommon::getErrorMessage("Customer not found")));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Get all customers
    /// </summary>
    /// <returns>Array of customer contracts</returns>
    public List getAllCustomers()
    {
        CustTable custTable;
        List customerList = new List(Types::Class);
        CustRESTCustomerContract contract;

        while select custTable
        {
            contract = new CustRESTCustomerContract(custTable);
            customerList.addEnd(contract);
        }

        return customerList;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Create a new customer
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="customerContract">Customer data contract</param>
    /// <returns>Created customer contract</returns>
    public CustRESTCustomerContract createCustomer(CustRESTCustomerContract _customerContract)
    {
        CustTable custTable;
        AccountNum accountNum;

        ttsBegin;

        // Generate new account number
        accountNum = NumberSeq::getNumFromId(NumberSeq::getNumberSequenceIdNum('Cust'));

        // Create new customer record
        custTable.AccountNum = accountNum;
        custTable.name(_customerContract.name());
        custTable.CustGroup = _customerContract.custGroup();
        custTable.Email = _customerContract.email();

        custTable.insert();

        ttsCommit;

        return new CustRESTCustomerContract(custTable);
    }
}
```

## Step 3: Create the Service Deployment Class

Now we need to create a class to deploy and register our service.

```xpp
/// <summary>
/// Deployment class for Customer REST service
/// </summary>
[AOTName("CustRESTServiceDeployment")]
class CustRESTServiceDeployment
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Deploys the Customer REST service
    /// </summary>
    public static void deployService()
    {
        AifServiceConfiguration aifServiceConfiguration;
        AifService aifService;
        AifEndpoint aifEndpoint;
        AifInboundPort inboundPort;
        AifEndpointActionPolicy endpointActionPolicy;
        AifServiceOperations serviceOperations;
        AifOperation operation;
        AifEndpointAction endpointAction;

        // Create service configuration if it doesn't exist
        select firstOnly aifServiceConfiguration
            where aifServiceConfiguration.Name == "CustRESTServiceConfig";

        if (!aifServiceConfiguration)
        {
            aifServiceConfiguration = AifUtil::createServiceConfiguration(
                "CustRESTServiceConfig",
                "Customer REST Service Configuration",
                AifConfigurationType::Endpoint,
                true,
                true);
        }

        // Create the service
        select firstOnly aifService
            where aifService.Name == "CustRESTService";

        if (!aifService)
        {
            aifService = AifUtil::createService(
                "CustRESTService",
                "Customer REST Service",
                classNum(CustRESTService),
                true);
        }

        // Create endpoint if it doesn't exist
        select firstOnly aifEndpoint
            where aifEndpoint.Name == "CustRESTEndpoint";

        if (!aifEndpoint)
        {
            aifEndpoint = AifUtil::createEndpoint(
                "CustRESTEndpoint",
                "Customer REST Endpoint",
                classNum(CustRESTService),
                AifEndpointType::Basic,
                AifBindingType::BasicHttp,
                AifAuthenticationType::Basic,
                AifEndpointAddressFormat::Uri,
                true);
        }

        // Create inbound port
        select firstOnly inboundPort
            where inboundPort.Name == "CustRESTInboundPort";

        if (!inboundPort)
        {
            inboundPort = AifUtil::createInboundPort(
                "CustRESTInboundPort",
                "Customer REST Inbound Port",
                aifEndpoint.RecId,
                aifService.RecId,
                aifServiceConfiguration.RecId,
                AifTransportType::NetTcp,
                "http://localhost:8201/DynamicsAx/Services/CustRESTService",
                AifActivationType::Private);
        }

        // Set endpoint address
        aifEndpoint.EndpointAddress = "http://localhost:8201/DynamicsAx/Services/CustRESTService";
        aifEndpoint.update();

        // Enable the service
        AifUtil::enableService(aifService.RecId);

        // Add service operations
        serviceOperations = AifUtil::getServiceOperations(aifService.RecId);

        // Add getCustomerByAccount operation
        operation = serviceOperations.getOperationByName("getCustomerByAccount");
        if (!operation)
        {
            operation = AifUtil::createServiceOperation(
                aifService.RecId,
                "getCustomerByAccount",
                classNum(CustRESTService),
                methodStr(CustRESTService, getCustomerByAccount));
        }

        // Add getAllCustomers operation
        operation = serviceOperations.getOperationByName("getAllCustomers");
        if (!operation)
        {
            operation = AifUtil::createServiceOperation(
                aifService.RecId,
                "getAllCustomers",
                classNum(CustRESTService),
                methodStr(CustRESTService, getAllCustomers));
        }

        // Add createCustomer operation
        operation = serviceOperations.getOperationByName("createCustomer");
        if (!operation)
        {
            operation = AifUtil::createServiceOperation(
                aifService.RecId,
                "createCustomer",
                classNum(CustRESTService),
                methodStr(CustRESTService, createCustomer));
        }

        // Add endpoint actions
        endpointActionPolicy = AifUtil::getEndpointActionPolicy(aifEndpoint.RecId);

        // Add action for getCustomerByAccount
        endpointAction = endpointActionPolicy.getEndpointActionByName("getCustomerByAccount");
        if (!endpointAction)
        {
            endpointAction = AifUtil::createEndpointAction(
                aifEndpoint.RecId,
                "getCustomerByAccount",
                "GET",
                "/Customers({AccountNum})");
        }

        // Add action for getAllCustomers
        endpointAction = endpointActionPolicy.getEndpointActionByName("getAllCustomers");
        if (!endpointAction)
        {
            endpointAction = AifUtil::createEndpointAction(
                aifEndpoint.RecId,
                "getAllCustomers",
                "GET",
                "/Customers");
        }

        // Add action for createCustomer
        endpointAction = endpointActionPolicy.getEndpointActionByName("createCustomer");
        if (!endpointAction)
        {
            endpointAction = AifUtil::createEndpointAction(
                aifEndpoint.RecId,
                "createCustomer",
                "POST",
                "/Customers");
        }

        Info("Customer REST Service deployed successfully!");
    }
}
```

## Step 4: Run the Deployment

To deploy the service, you would run the following job:

```xpp
static void deployCustRESTService()
{
    CustRESTServiceDeployment::deployService();
}
```

## Step 5: Test the Service

Once deployed, you can test the service using a tool like Postman or by calling it from code.

Example URLs would be:
- GET http://localhost:8201/DynamicsAx/Services/CustRESTService/Customers - Get all customers
- GET http://localhost:8201/DynamicsAx/Services/CustRESTService/Customers(1000) - Get customer with account 1000
- POST http://localhost:8201/DynamicsAx/Services/CustRESTService/Customers - Create a new customer

## Important Notes:

1. **Security**: Make sure to implement proper security in a production environment.
2. **Error Handling**: The example includes basic error handling, but you should expand it for production use.
3. **Port Configuration**: The port number (8201) may need to be adjusted based on your installation.
4. **Authentication**: The example uses basic authentication, but you may want to implement more secure authentication methods.
5. **Performance**: For large datasets, consider implementing paging for the getAllCustomers method.

This example provides a complete foundation for creating a custom REST service in Dynamics AX. You can extend it with more operations and data as needed.

